export const EXAM_CLOZE: ExamCloze[] = [{"id":"2024-06-1","source":"2024年06月 · 第1套","paragraphs":["It’s well known that physical exercise is beneficial not just to physical health but also to mental health. Yet whereas most countries have        26 , evidence-backed guidelines on the type and intensity of exercise      27 for various physical health benefits, such guidelines do not yet exist for exercise and mood. This is    28     due to a lack of necessary evidence. However, a new systematic review brings us usefully up-to-date on the current findings in this area.","Before      29     into some of the key take-aways, an important        30     made in the review is between aerobic exercise and anaerobic. The former       31 such things as walking, jogging and cycling and means exercising in such a way that your body is able to use oxygen to burn fat for energy. In contrast, anaerobic exercise—such as lifting heavy weights—is of such 32 intensity that your body does not have time to use oxygen to create energy and so instead it breaks down glucose (葡萄糖) in your blood or muscles.","Beginning first with the influence of exercise intensity on the mood benefits of aerobic exercise, the researchers, led by John Chan at Shenzhen University, found     33 results from 19 relevant studies. Some favoured higher intensity, others low, while seven studies found that intensity made no      34 to mood benefits.","In relation to the intensity of anaerobic exercise, however, the results were far clearer— the optimum (最佳选择) for improving mood is                  35   intensity, perhaps because low intensity is too dull while high intensity is too unpleasant."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"constitutes"},{"letter":"B","word":"contradictory"},{"letter":"C","word":"decision"},{"letter":"D","word":"detailed"},{"letter":"E","word":"difference"},{"letter":"F","word":"dipping"},{"letter":"G","word":"distinction"},{"letter":"H","word":"falling"},{"letter":"I","word":"involves"},{"letter":"J","word":"moderate"},{"letter":"K","word":"notified"},{"letter":"L","word":"partly"},{"letter":"M","word":"required"},{"letter":"N","word":"traditionally"},{"letter":"O","word":"vigorous"}],"answers":["D","M","L","F","G","I","O","B","E","J"]},{"id":"2024-06-2","source":"2024年06月 · 第2套","paragraphs":["A team of researchers led by Priyanka Joshi examined the degree to which men and women relied on “communicative abstraction” to verbally convey their ideas and emotions. Communicative abstraction, according to the researchers, reflects the tendency of people to use “abstract speech that focuses on the broader picture and 26        purpose of action rather than concrete speech focusing on details and the means of         27     action.” Interestingly, they found that men were far more likely to speak in the abstract than were women.","To arrive at this    28    , the researchers examined the linguistic (语言的) patterns of men and women in over 600,000 blog posts written on websites. To do this, the researchers computed abstractness ratings for         29     40,000 commonly used words in the English language. Words considered to be concrete could be easily visualized, such as “table” or “chair”. Words that were more          30      to visualize, for example, “justice” or “morality” were considered to be more abstract. They found that men used       31 more abstract language in their blog posts.","What is the       32    of this effect? The researchers suggest that power differences between the genders— that is, men having more power in society—might be a key determinant (决定因素). For instance, in a follow-up study conducted with a sample of 300 students, the researchers     33     power dynamics in an interpersonal setting to see if this would influence communicative abstraction. They found that participants in a high-power interviewer role were more likely to give abstract descriptions of behaviors than were participants in a low-power interviewee role. This suggests that communicating more abstractly does not reflect a         34 tendency of men or women but rather        35 within specific contexts."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"approximately"},{"letter":"B","word":"attaining"},{"letter":"C","word":"conclusion"},{"letter":"D","word":"difficult"},{"letter":"E","word":"emerges"},{"letter":"F","word":"fixed"},{"letter":"G","word":"ignored"},{"letter":"H","word":"legally"},{"letter":"I","word":"manipulated"},{"letter":"J","word":"recommended"},{"letter":"K","word":"refraining"},{"letter":"L","word":"signals"},{"letter":"M","word":"significantly"},{"letter":"N","word":"source"},{"letter":"O","word":"ultimate"}],"answers":["O","B","C","A","D","M","N","I","F","E"]},{"id":"2024-06-3","source":"2024年06月 · 第3套","paragraphs":["Over the coming decades, millions of jobs will be threatened by robotics and artificial intelligence. Despite intensive academic        26 on these developments, there has been little study on how workers         27     to being replaced through technology.","To find out, business researchers at TUM and Erasmus University Rotterdam conducted 11 studies and surveys with over 2,000 persons from several countries.","The findings show: In principle, most people view it more            28   when workers are replaced by other people than by robots or intelligent software. This preference              29 , however, when it refers to people’s own jobs. When that is the case, the majority of workers find it less upsetting to see their own jobs go to robots than to other employees. In the long term, however, the same people see machines as more threatening to their future role in the workforce. These effects can also be observed among people who have recently become unemployed.","The researchers were able to identify the causes behind these       30 paradoxical results, too: People tend to           31       themselves less with machines than with other people. Consequently, being replaced by a robot or software 32 less of a threat to their feeling of self-worth. This reduced self-threat could even be observed when participants assumed that they were being replaced by other employees who relied on technological abilities such as artificial intelligence in their work.","“Even when unemployment results from the              33 of new technologies, people still judge it in a social context,” says Christoph Fuchs, one of the authors of the study. “It is important to understand these         34 effects when trying to manage the massive changes in the working world to minimize           35 in society.”"],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"compare"},{"letter":"B","word":"contradicts"},{"letter":"C","word":"conventional"},{"letter":"D","word":"debate"},{"letter":"E","word":"disruptions"},{"letter":"F","word":"drastically"},{"letter":"G","word":"favorably"},{"letter":"H","word":"guarantee"},{"letter":"I","word":"introduction"},{"letter":"J","word":"modifications"},{"letter":"K","word":"poses"},{"letter":"L","word":"psychological"},{"letter":"M","word":"react"},{"letter":"N","word":"reverses"},{"letter":"O","word":"seemingly"}],"answers":["D","M","G","N","O","A","K","I","L","E"]},{"id":"2025-06-1","source":"2025年06月 · 第1套","paragraphs":["Psychologists have long been interested in how we construct our identities and the sorts of strategies that we use to present ourselves in society. New findings suggest that the kinds of 26 and strategic self-presentation behaviour we see in adults appear at a much younger age than 27 known.","Research shows that a child's awareness of social standing comes from adults. Like grown-ups, kids want to be 28 by those they admire. Interactive experiences may provide opportunities for children to learn about what 29 a desirable reputation and the kinds of strategies that are effective for 30 a good reputation in their social environment.","Five-year-olds aren't just aware of their reputations, they also behave strategically to alter their outward image. They will 31 their behaviour in order to appear moral or socially good in the eyes of key observers. While we know that adults use a large variety of attributes to manage and create impressions, we don't yet know whether children 32 and use the fact that different attributes are valuable at different times to different 33. It's important for us to further consider where in this process children succeed in controlling their reputation and where they 34.","A question to think about is, “What happens even earlier than age five?” Children don't just show up to the first day of kindergarten and have the idea of reputation pop 35 into existence. The logical question to ask is, “What happens even earlier?”"],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"accepted"},{"letter":"B","word":"audiences"},{"letter":"C","word":"building"},{"letter":"D","word":"complex"},{"letter":"E","word":"constitutes"},{"letter":"F","word":"deputies"},{"letter":"G","word":"previously"},{"letter":"H","word":"revolving"},{"letter":"I","word":"samples"},{"letter":"J","word":"selected"},{"letter":"K","word":"solemn"},{"letter":"L","word":"struggle"},{"letter":"M","word":"suddenly"},{"letter":"N","word":"understand"},{"letter":"O","word":"vary"}],"answers":["D","G","A","E","C","O","N","B","L","M"]},{"id":"2025-06-2","source":"2025年06月 · 第2套","paragraphs":["Sir Alfred Hitchcock was an English movie director and producer. Famously 26 to as “The Master of Suspense”, Hitchcock is one of the most influential filmmakers in the history of 27. He was an extraordinary director who entertained his audience with 28 and gripping suspense movies.","His fascination with crime began at an early age when he was 29 by his father who made him spend a few minutes inside a prison for his misconduct. Hence, his movies are 30 of the guilt and innocence of the wrongdoer and the victim. He had a gift for creating stories that consisted of deceit, robbery, murder, corruption, and other criminal 31 with incredible plot twists in the storyline. The principal characters in his movies were often ordinary people 32 in unwanted and unavoidable situations.","He was 33 productive and his amazing body of work is considered fascinating by the critics. Most of his movies have 34 the test of time and are considered to be masterpieces. He is also remembered by other filmmakers, for he continues to inspire them to be passionate about their work. He is also 35 by people around the world for his entertaining and exciting stories."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"caught"},{"letter":"B","word":"cinema"},{"letter":"C","word":"engaging"},{"letter":"D","word":"graphically"},{"letter":"E","word":"highly"},{"letter":"F","word":"incentive"},{"letter":"G","word":"instincts"},{"letter":"H","word":"offences"},{"letter":"I","word":"punished"},{"letter":"J","word":"referred"},{"letter":"K","word":"stood"},{"letter":"L","word":"symbolic"},{"letter":"M","word":"tuned"},{"letter":"N","word":"visually"},{"letter":"O","word":"worshipped"}],"answers":["J","B","C","I","L","H","A","E","K","O"]},{"id":"2025-06-3","source":"2025年06月 · 第3套","paragraphs":["The human brain has the ability to constantly form new networks and connections between brain cells. This means the brain has an almost magical ability to change. This characteristic is 26 apparent in a new study, focusing on people who underwent a hemispherectomy, a surgical procedure in which half of the brain is removed to treat illness.","The findings showed that, despite missing half of this critical 27, participants could function well. This was because the 28 half of their brain strengthened. In fact, researchers found that connections—and thus communication—between parts of different brain networks are actually stronger in people who had hemispherectomies than in people with intact brains. This 29 that the brain is able to compensate for loss of certain brain structure.","There are many other cases in the medical 30 that document the brain's amazing ability to 31. For example, a young boy had a significant portion of his brain removed for medical reasons, which included the part of the brain 32 for sight. But a few years after his surgery, scientists found that he could 33 see. They determined that this was because other parts of his brain took over the missing parts' 34 tasks. Another study involved people who could smell, despite missing the region in the brain that processes information about smells. Though they are not sure how these individuals 35 the ability to smell, scientists believe it is possible that another part of the brain took on that task."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"adapt"},{"letter":"B","word":"hardly"},{"letter":"C","word":"indicates"},{"letter":"D","word":"insist"},{"letter":"E","word":"literature"},{"letter":"F","word":"organ"},{"letter":"G","word":"particularly"},{"letter":"H","word":"remaining"},{"letter":"I","word":"responsible"},{"letter":"J","word":"retained"},{"letter":"K","word":"still"},{"letter":"L","word":"strategy"},{"letter":"M","word":"transformed"},{"letter":"N","word":"underlines"},{"letter":"O","word":"visual"}],"answers":["G","F","H","C","E","A","I","K","O","J"]},{"id":"2025-12-1","source":"2025年12月 · 第1套","paragraphs":["People tend to want as many choices as possible. They believe this will maximize their 26 of making the best decision. But research shows that, when it comes to actually making a 27 from all of these choices, people can become 28 and avoid making a decision altogether. Even worse, when people finally do decide, they are generally less satisfied with their decision and feel more regretful over whatever choice they made.","Why does this happen? Research shows that when people choose from many options, they 29 more in the decision, but feel less confident in their ability to decide well. In other words, when we are 30 with more choices, making the “right” or “correct” decision begins to feel more 31 and, at the same time, more difficult to do. This may contribute to the deep fear that we will make the wrong decision.","How can we solve this problem? I believe this fear could be tempered by putting decisions into perspective. It might help to remember that many of the choices you make, such as what to have for lunch, will not 32 much in the future and that, even more important choices, like accepting a new job, can 33 be changed. It could also help to 34 these situations with clear guidelines and ideas of what you want from the 35 of options, which can narrow the possible choices, and also make you more confident about your ability to make the right decision."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"approximately"},{"letter":"B","word":"case"},{"letter":"C","word":"chance"},{"letter":"D","word":"confused"},{"letter":"E","word":"crucial"},{"letter":"F","word":"deposited"},{"letter":"G","word":"enter"},{"letter":"H","word":"invest"},{"letter":"I","word":"matter"},{"letter":"J","word":"presented"},{"letter":"K","word":"range"},{"letter":"L","word":"regular"},{"letter":"M","word":"seize"},{"letter":"N","word":"selection"},{"letter":"O","word":"ultimately"}],"answers":["C","N","D","H","J","E","I","O","G","K"]},{"id":"2025-12-2","source":"2025年12月 · 第2套","paragraphs":["Some music inspires you to move your feet, some inspires you to get out there and change the world. In any case, it's 26 to say that music moves people in special ways.","If you're especially into a piece of music, your brain does something called Autonomous Sensory Meridian Response (ASMR), which 27 to you like a sting in your brain.","It turns out that ASMR is pretty special. According to a 28 published study in the Journal of Prevention of Alzheimer's Disease, the part of your brain responsible for ASMR doesn't get lost to Alzheimer's. Alzheimer's 29 to put people into layers of confusion, and the study confirms that music can sometimes 30 lift people out of the Alzheimer's haze and bring them back to (at least a likeness of) normality...if only for a short while. ASMR is powerful stuff!","This phenomenon has been 31 several times but rarely studied properly. One of the most famous examples of this is the story of 92-year-old Henry Dryer, who comes out of dementia (痴呆) while listening to songs from his youth.","Jeff Anderson, associate professor in Radiology at the University of Utah and 32 author on the study, says “In our society, the diagnoses of dementia are 33 resources to the maximum. No one says playing music will be a cure for Alzheimer's disease, but it might make the symptoms more 34, decrease the cost of care and improve a patient's 35 of life.”"],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"actually"},{"letter":"B","word":"consequently"},{"letter":"C","word":"contributing"},{"letter":"D","word":"fair"},{"letter":"E","word":"feels"},{"letter":"F","word":"manageable"},{"letter":"G","word":"mends"},{"letter":"H","word":"observed"},{"letter":"I","word":"phase"},{"letter":"J","word":"plotting"},{"letter":"K","word":"quality"},{"letter":"L","word":"recently"},{"letter":"M","word":"taxing"},{"letter":"N","word":"tends"},{"letter":"O","word":"yielded"}],"answers":["D","E","L","N","A","H","C","M","F","K"]},{"id":"2025-12-3","source":"2025年12月 · 第3套","paragraphs":["Earth Day is an annual celebration that honors the achievements of the environmental movement and raises awareness of the need to protect Earth's natural resources for future generations. Earth Day is celebrated on April 22 in the United States and on either April 22 or the day the spring equinox (春分) occurs throughout the 26 of the world.","Environmental activism during the 1960s 27 Wisconsin Senator Gaylord Nelson to create a 28 celebration uniting the environmental movement. With the help of Denis Hayes, a graduate student at Harvard University, Nelson organized the first Earth Day on April 22, 1970, educating participants in the 29 of environmental protection. Attended by 20 million people across the United States, the event 30 support for legislation such as the Clean Air Act and the Endangered Species Act.","In 1990, Hayes organized a global Earth Day, with more than 200 million participants in 140 countries. Earth Day now brings 31 citizens and activists from around the world to raise awareness and take action regarding such environmental 32 as global warming and renewable energy.","Today, the Earth Day Network, which rallies more than 20,000 33 and organizations in 190 countries, supports the Earth Day mission year-round. This mission is founded on the proposition that all people, regardless of race, gender, income, or 34, have a moral right to a healthy, sustainable environment. The Earth Day Network 35 this mission through education, public policy, and activism campaigns."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"concerns"},{"letter":"B","word":"expansion"},{"letter":"C","word":"forth"},{"letter":"D","word":"geography"},{"letter":"E","word":"importance"},{"letter":"F","word":"imposed"},{"letter":"G","word":"inspired"},{"letter":"H","word":"national"},{"letter":"I","word":"partners"},{"letter":"J","word":"potential"},{"letter":"K","word":"pursues"},{"letter":"L","word":"rescues"},{"letter":"M","word":"rest"},{"letter":"N","word":"strengthened"},{"letter":"O","word":"together"}],"answers":["M","G","H","E","N","O","A","I","D","K"]},{"id":"2026-06-1","source":"2026年06月 · 第1套","paragraphs":["One of the biggest controversies over the Industrial Revolution is how it affected the working class. The oldest debates were over whether the standards of living rose or fell. Those that believed they fell claimed that the capitalists 26 every ounce of surplus they could from the working class. Those that believed the standards of living rose claimed that the environment was consumer-friendly, with more and more goods 27 to the working class every year.","Today's historians agree that overall, the standards of living 28 . They do not agree, however, on when this improvement 29 .","In an effort to solve this controversy, historians have attempted to define 30 what \"standard of living\" means. They all seem to agree that it should mean happiness, but happiness is impossible to measure. Instead, historians 31 use \"real income\" as the measure for the standards of living. Real income is money 32 and then adjusted according to the cost of living. However, it does not take into account unemployment, pollution, health, life expectancy, or free time.","After 33 debate and analysis of the average income, historians have agreed to disagree on whether there was rapid or slow economic growth during the Industrial Revolution. Instead, they have decided to 34 how the Industrial Revolution was affected by other events. They have determined that the Industrial Revolution had an overall positive 35 , but it quite possibly was neutralized by negative events such as wars, high taxes, and rapid population growth."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"available"},{"letter":"B","word":"deteriorating"},{"letter":"C","word":"earned"},{"letter":"D","word":"effect"},{"letter":"E","word":"enhance"},{"letter":"F","word":"exactly"},{"letter":"G","word":"exhausting"},{"letter":"H","word":"experience"},{"letter":"I","word":"increased"},{"letter":"J","word":"interpret"},{"letter":"K","word":"occurred"},{"letter":"L","word":"peculiar"},{"letter":"M","word":"probably"},{"letter":"N","word":"squeezed"},{"letter":"O","word":"typically"}],"answers":["N","A","I","K","F","O","C","G","J","D"]},{"id":"2026-06-2","source":"2026年06月 · 第2套","paragraphs":["It may sound surprising, but people who are supersensitive to coffee’s bitter taste actually drink more of it, a new study finds.","This sensitivity isn’t 26 a matter of taste, either, but rather is influenced by a person’s genetic makeup, the researchers said in the study.","“You’d expect that people who are particularly sensitive to the bitter taste of caffeine would drink less coffee,” said study senior researcher Marilyn Cornelis. “The 27 results of our study suggest coffee consumers acquire a taste for or an ability to detect the bitterness of caffeine due to the learned positive 28 brought out by caffeine.”","Put another way, people who have a 29 ability to taste the bitterness of coffee learn to associate “good things with it,” Cornelis said. This finding is surprising, given that bitterness often serves as a warning mechanism to 30 people to spit out harmful substances, scientists said.","Researchers conducted the study to understand how genetics influences people’s 31 of tea, coffee and alcohol which tend to taste bitter, said lead study researcher Jue Sheng Ong.","“While all bitter flavors may seem the same, we 32 the bitterness of Brussels sprouts (抱子甘蓝), quinine (奎宁) and caffeine 33,” Ong told Live Science. “The degree to which we find these flavors bitter is, in part, determined by your genes.”","People with the genes to taste the bitterness of green vegetables are more likely to prefer tea to coffee. In 34 , people who were more sensitive to quinine’s bitter flavor and those found in green vegetables tended to 35 coffee."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"addition"},{"letter":"B","word":"approximately"},{"letter":"C","word":"avoid"},{"letter":"D","word":"consumption"},{"letter":"E","word":"converted"},{"letter":"F","word":"convince"},{"letter":"G","word":"heightened"},{"letter":"H","word":"omission"},{"letter":"I","word":"opposite"},{"letter":"J","word":"perceive"},{"letter":"K","word":"prospect"},{"letter":"L","word":"reinforcement"},{"letter":"M","word":"separately"},{"letter":"N","word":"simply"},{"letter":"O","word":"targeted"}],"answers":["N","I","L","G","F","D","J","M","A","C"]},{"id":"2026-06-3","source":"2026年06月 · 第3套","paragraphs":["Junk-food lovers who try to cut back on fries or chocolate may experience symptoms similar to drug withdrawal, a new study suggests.","Researchers found that people attempting to cut down on eating highly processed foods experience some of the same 26 and psychological symptoms—such as mood swings, anxiety, headaches and poor sleep—as those 27 smoking cigarettes or using drugs, according to the study.","The new study 28 the first evidence that these withdrawal-like symptoms can occur when people cut down on highly processed foods, said lead study author Erica Schulte.","Based on the participants’ self-reported symptoms, withdrawal symptoms were 29 more intense between the second and fifth days after attempting to reduce junk-food consumption, which 30 the time span people live through during drug withdrawal.","The idea that food may be addictive after “heavy” use by some individuals is a 31 subject, Schulte said. Although prior studies in animals and humans have shown some biological and behavioral similarities between substance-use disorders and addictive-like consumption of highly processed foods, no studies have looked at whether reducing junk food can 32 withdrawal symptoms in people, she noted.","Raising 33 that people may experience irritability (烦躁) or headaches when cutting down on junk food can help individuals 34 coping strategies in advance, Schulte noted. The findings may also 35 light on the barriers people face when changing eating habits—barriers that may play a role in people dropping out of treatments, she said."],"bank":[{"letter":"A","word":"awareness"},{"letter":"B","word":"canceling"},{"letter":"C","word":"controversial"},{"letter":"D","word":"emptiness"},{"letter":"E","word":"monstrous"},{"letter":"F","word":"offers"},{"letter":"G","word":"parallels"},{"letter":"H","word":"permanently"},{"letter":"I","word":"physical"},{"letter":"J","word":"prepare"},{"letter":"K","word":"prospects"},{"letter":"L","word":"quitting"},{"letter":"M","word":"shed"},{"letter":"N","word":"significantly"},{"letter":"O","word":"trigger"}],"answers":["I","L","F","N","G","C","O","A","J","M"]}]

export const EXAM_TRANSLATION: ExamTranslation[] = [{"id":"2024-06-1","source":"2024年06月 · 第1套","prompt":"四合院（siheyuan）是中国一种传统的住宅建筑，其特点是房屋建造在一个院子的四周，将院子合围在中间。四合院通常冬暖夏凉，环境舒适，尤其适合大家庭居住。四合院在中国各地有多种类型，其中以北京的四合院最为典型。如今，随着现代城市的发展，传统的四合院已逐渐减少，但因其独特的建筑风格，四合院对中国文化的传承和中国历史的研究具有重","ref":"Siheyuan is a kind of traditional Chinese residential building, which is characterized by houses built around a courtyard, enclosing the courtyard in the middle. Siheyuan is usually warm in winter and cool in summer, offering a comfortable environment, especially suitable for large families to live in. There are many types of Siheyuan in different parts of China, of which the most typical one is in Beijing. Nowadays, with the development of modern cities, the number of traditional Siheyuan has gradually decreased, but because of its unique architectural style, Siheyuan is of great significance to the inheritance of Chinese culture and the study of Chinese history."},{"id":"2024-06-2","source":"2024年06月 · 第2套","prompt":"农历（the lunar calendar）起源于数千年前的中国，根据太阳和月亮的运行规律制定。长期以来，农历在农业生产和人们日常生活中发挥着重要作用。古人依据农历记录日期、安排农活，以便最有效地利用自然资源和气候条件，提高农作物的产量和质量。中国的春节、中秋节等传统节日的日期都基于农历。农历是中国传统文化的重要组成部分，当今依然广为","ref":"The lunar calendar, which originated in China thousands of years ago, was formulated based on the movements of the sun and the moon. For a long time, the lunar calendar has played an important role in agricultural production and people’s daily lives. Ancient people recorded dates and arranged farm work according to the lunar calendar in order to make the most efficient use of natural resources and climatic conditions to improve the yield and quality of crops. The Chinese Spring Festival, Mid-Autumn Festival and other traditional festivals are based on the lunar calendar. It is an important component of traditional Chinese culture and is still widely used today."},{"id":"2024-06-3","source":"2024年06月 · 第3套","prompt":"汉语中的“福”字（the character fu）表示幸福和好运，是中国传统文化中最常用的吉祥（auspicious）符号之一。人们通常将一个大大的福字写在红纸上，寓意期盼家庭幸福、社会安定、国家昌盛。春节贴福字是民间由来已久的习俗。为了欢庆春节，家家户户都会将福字贴在门上或墙上，表达对幸福生活的向往、对美好未来的期待。人们有时还将福字倒过来贴，表示幸福已到、好运已到。","ref":"The Chinese character “fu”, signifying happiness and good luck, is one of the most commonly used auspicious symbols in traditional Chinese culture. People usually write a big character of fu on red paper, which means that they look forward to family happiness, social stability and national prosperity. Posting the character of fu during the Spring Festival is a long- standing folk custom. In order to celebrate the Spring Festival, every family will put the character of fu on the doors or walls to express the yearning for a happy life and the expectation for a better future. People sometimes put the character of fu upside down, indicating that happiness and good luck have arrived."},{"id":"2024-12-1","source":"2024年12月 · 第1套","prompt":"中国政府十分重视环境保护。近年来，中国在减少空气、水和土壤污染上取得了显著成效。为了不断改善人们的生活环境，中国采取了一系列有效措施，包括大力发展清洁能源，改善公共交通，推广共享单车，实施垃圾分类。通过这些措施，中国的城市和农村正在绿起来、美起来。中国还积极参与国际合作，为全球环境保护做出了重要贡献。","ref":"The Chinese government places great emphasis on environmental protection. In recent years, China has made remarkable strides in reducing air, water and soil pollution. The country has adopted a series of effective measures to continuously improve the living environment of its people, including the vigorous development of clean energy, enhancement of public transportation, popularization of shared bikes and implementation of garbage sorting. Thanks to these actions, both urban and rural areas in China are becoming greener and more beautiful. Besides, China is an active participant in international cooperation, contributing significantly to global environmental protection.","tipsLabel":"难点注释","tips":"1. 第一句较短，属于讲述客观事实的句子，翻译时句子时态应选用一般现在时，谓语动词采用第三人称单数形式。“十分重视”是四级段落翻译的高频考点，可译为place great emphasis on。\n2. 第二句句首的“近年来”提示本句应使用现在完成时。翻译时要注意调整语序，先翻译句子的主干“……中国……取得了显著成效”，即…China has made remarkable strides…；然后再翻译次要信息“在减少空气、水和土壤污染上”，即in reducing air, water and soil pollution。\n3. 第三句较长，翻译之前需要先分析句子结构。翻译时可将“中国采取了一系列有效措施”作为句子主干译出；“为了不断改善人们的生活环境”可处理为不定式结构作目的状语；“包括”可译为介词including，与后面的内容一起构成介词短语；“大力发展清洁能源，改善公共交通，推广共享单车，实施垃圾分类”是四个动宾短语，翻译时可以进行词性转换，处理为名词短语，体现出英语静态的语言特征，如参考译文所示。\n4. 第四句中的“正在”表明本句应使用现在进行时；“通过这些措施”可按字面意思译为Through these measures，也可以把句子的逻辑关系显化，译为Thanks to these actions，用actions代替前文的measures，使译文用词富于变化。“绿起来、美起来”可以处理为现在进行时与形容词的比较级结构相结合的形式，即are becoming greener and more beautiful。\n5. 第五句包含两个分句，翻译时可以把第二个分句处理为现在分词结构作状语，如参考译文所示。也可以采用并列的谓语结构译出，即“Besides, China is an active participant in international cooperation and contributes significantly to global environmental protection.”"},{"id":"2024-12-2","source":"2024年12月 · 第2套","prompt":"近年来，中国新能源汽车产业发展迅速。目前，中国新能源汽车年产量已高达近千万辆，占全球市场份额超过60%，出口量不断创出新高。中国政府通过加大资金投入和政策引导，鼓励新能源汽车企业进行技术创新，不断提高产品在市场上的竞争力。中国新能源汽车产业的发展不仅有力推动了国内经济发展，也为全球新能源利用和环境保护做出了积极贡献。","ref":"In recent years, China's new energy vehicle industry has witnessed rapid growth. With an annual production close to 10 million units, China now holds over 60% of the global market share for new energy vehicles, and its export volume has been continuously reaching new highs. The Chinese government is encouraging new energy vehicle enterprises to carry out technological innovation and constantly enhance the market competitiveness of their products by increasing financial investment and providing policy guidance. The development of China's new energy vehicle industry has not only vigorously promoted domestic economic growth but also made a positive contribution to the global adoption of new energy and environmental protection.","tipsLabel":"难点注释","tips":"1. 第一句较短，在翻译时，由句首的“近年来”可知本句时态宜选用现在完成时。在翻译“发展”这一动词时，可以进行词性转换，处理为抽象名词，体现出英语静态的语言特征，如参考译文所示。本句增译witnessed，使译文更生动。\n2. 第二句较长，在翻译时，可将“年产量已高达近千万辆”处理为with结构置于句首，将“占全球市场份额超过60%”译为holds over 60% of the global market share，将“新能源汽车”译为介词短语for new energy vehicles作后置定语；“出口量不断创出新高”可处理为由and连接的并列句，时态选用现在完成进行时，其中“出口量”可译为export volume，“创出新高”可译为reach new highs。\n3. 第三句包含三个分句，在翻译时可将“鼓励新能源汽车企业进行技术创新”和“不断提高产品在市场上的竞争力”译为句子主干，“技术创新”可译为technological innovation，“市场上的竞争力”可译为the market competitiveness；“通过加大资金投入和政策引导”可译为介词by引导的方式状语，翻译时应在“政策引导”前增译provide以平衡句子结构，即by increasing financial investment and providing policy guidance。\n4. 第四句中的两个分句都描述了新能源汽车产业发展带来的好处，因此可以处理为not only…but also…结构。在翻译“为全球新能源利用和环境保护做出了积极贡献”时应先翻译“为……做出了积极贡献”，即make a positive contribution to…；再将“全球新能源利用和环境保护”译为由and连接的并列结构，即the global adoption of new energy and environmental protection。"},{"id":"2024-12-3","source":"2024年12月 · 第3套","prompt":"敦煌莫高窟（Mogao Grottoes）数字展示中心于2014年开放启用，是莫高窟保护利用工程的重要组成部分。展示中心采用数字技术和多媒体展示手段，使游客进入洞窟参观之前就能了解莫高窟的历史文化，鉴赏莫高窟的艺术经典。这将减少开放洞窟的数量，缩短游客在洞窟内的逗留时间，减轻参观对莫高窟造成的影响，以使这一世界文化遗产得到妥善保护、长久利用。","ref":"The Dunhuang Mogao Grottoes Digital Exhibition Center, which was opened in 2014, is an integral part of the conservation and utilization project of the Mogao Grottoes. The exhibition center enables visitors to learn about the culture of the Mogao Grottoes and appreciate its art classics before entering the actual grottoes by adopting digital technology and multimedia presentations. This approach helps to limit the number of grottoes open to the public, reduce the duration of visitors' stay inside and minimize the impact on the Mogao Grottoes, so as to ensure this world cultural heritage site is properly protected and sustainably utilized.","tipsLabel":"难点注释","tips":"1. 第一句包含两个分句，翻译时要注意时态。第一个分句中的时间状语“2014年”表明时态应该使用一般过去时；第二个分句描述客观事实，因此时态应使用一般现在时。根据句子的逻辑关系，第一个分句中的“于2014年开放启用”可翻译为非限制性定语从句；第二个分句可处理为主句，如参考译文所示。“敦煌莫高窟数字展示中心”可以译为The Dunhuang Mogao Grottoes Digital Exhibition Center。“开放”和“启用”语义重复，可以合译为was opened或者was put into use。\n2. 第二句较长，包含三个分句。“采用数字技术和多媒体展示手段”可翻译为介词短语by adopting digital technology and multimedia presentations，作为方式状语置于句末。“展示中心……使游客……能了解莫高窟的历史文化，鉴赏莫高窟的艺术经典”可译为句子主干，使用sth. enable(s) sb. to do sth.这一结构，即The exhibition center enables visitors to learn about the culture of the Mogao Grottoes and appreciate its art classics；“进入洞窟参观之前”可翻译为before entering the actual grottoes，作时间状语。\n3. 第三句较长，翻译时需要理清句子之间的逻辑关系。前三个分句中的“减少”“缩短”和“减轻”可翻译为并列谓语；最后一个分句可翻译为目的状语，使用被动语态结构，即so as to ensure this world cultural heritage site is properly protected and sustainably utilized。也可以将原句拆分，把最后一个分句单独译为一句，即“This is to ensure the proper preservation and sustainable use of the world cultural heritage site.”。在细节处理方面，本句涉及增译和减译翻译技巧的运用，比如“减少开放洞窟的数量”可译为limit the number of grottoes open to the public，增译to the public；“缩短游客在洞窟内的逗留时间”可译为reduce the duration of visitors' stay inside，减译“洞窟”；“减轻参观对莫高窟造成的影响”可译为minimize the impact on the Mogao Grottoes，减译“参观”；“这一世界文化遗产”可译为this world cultural heritage site，增译site。通过增译和减译，使译文更加准确、简洁。"},{"id":"2025-06-1","source":"2025年06月 · 第1套","prompt":"被誉为“杂交水稻(hybrid rice)之父”的袁隆平和他的科研团队克服重重困难，研发出了一种超级杂交水稻。这项技术获得了举世公认的巨大成功。通过这项技术的应用，水稻抗旱抗病能力更强，能适应不同的气候和土壤条件，产量可提高20-30%。超级杂交水稻营养丰富，口感更佳。目前，这项技术已经在许多国家得到广泛应用，为全球粮食安全做出了重大贡献。","ref":"Yuan Longping, known globally as the “Father of Hybrid Rice,” and his research team overcame numerous challenges to successfully develop a super hybrid rice variety. This technology has been universally recognized as a tremendous success. Through the application of this technology, the rice exhibits stronger drought and disease resistance, adapts to diverse climatic and soil conditions, and achieves a 20-30% increase in yield. The super hybrid rice is also more nutritious and has a superior taste. Currently, the technology has been widely applied in many countries, making significant contributions to global food security.","tips":"1. 本句除了难词译注中列出的重点词汇之外，还应注意分析前后分句逻辑关系。通过分析可知，“研发出了一种超级杂交水稻”是“克服重重困难”的结果，因此应将“克服重重困难”作为子句谓语，翻译成overcame numerous challenges，而“研发出了一种超级杂交水稻”翻译成表示结果的不定式短语，即to successfully develop a super hybrid rice variety，增译successfully一词是为了突出这一结果的成功性，更符合英文表达习惯。\n2. 本句要强调的是“举世公认”和“巨大成功”两个要素，而且要在同一个英文句子中体现出来，因此首先应使用be recognized as a success这一基本短语来表达，再分别对recognized和success进行修饰，故“获得了举世公认的巨大成功”应翻译为has been universally recognized as a tremendous success。\n3. “通过这项技术的应用”是方式状语，应翻译为介词短语Through the application of this technology；“抗旱抗病能力更强”“能适应不同的气候和土壤条件”“产量可提高20-30%”叙述的是该水稻的优点，应该翻译为三个并列的谓语部分，即exhibits stronger drought and disease resistance, adapts to diverse climatic and soil conditions, and achieves a 20-30% increase in yield。\n4. “营养丰富，口感更佳”是对“超级杂交水稻”特点的描述，根据英文表达习惯，应翻译成谓语，而两者为并列结构，根据“口感更佳”可知，“营养丰富”暗含比较意味，应翻译成比较级结构，故二者翻译为is also more nutritious and has a superior taste，增译also一词是为了与前一句衔接，体现前后句的逻辑关系。\n5. 前一个分句“目前，这项技术已经在许多国家得到广泛应用”是主体，应翻译为Currently, the technology has been widely applied in many countries，而“为全球粮食安全做出了重大贡献”为补充说明性内容，表示伴随情况，故使用现在分词短语来翻译，即making significant contributions to global food security。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2025-06-2","source":"2025年06月 · 第2套","prompt":"近年来，中国东北地区正在大力开发冰雪资源。例如，哈尔滨利用丰富的冰雪资源打造了极具地方特色的“冰雪大世界”，让游客在欣赏冰雪之美的同时也能体验当地独特的民俗文化。如今，曾令人畏惧的冰天雪地正吸引着四面八方的游客，成为深受欢迎的旅游胜地。冰雪旅游业正为当地的经济发展做出越来越大的贡献。","ref":"In recent years, Northeast China has been vigorously developing its ice and snow resources. For instance, Harbin has created the highly distinctive “Ice and Snow World” by leveraging its abundant ice and snow resources, allowing visitors to appreciate the beauty of ice and snow while experiencing the region's unique folk culture. What was once an intimidating frozen landscape is now attracting tourists from all directions, becoming a highly popular tourist destination. The ice and snow tourism industry is making an increasingly significant contribution to local economic development.","tips":"1. 第一句：“近年来”翻译为In recent years；“中国东北地区”翻译为Northeast China；“正在大力开发”翻译为has been vigorously developing。\n2. 第二句：本句较长，先进行拆分，主体句是“哈尔滨利用丰富的冰雪资源打造了极具地方特色的‘冰雪大世界’”，翻译为Harbin has created the highly distinctive “Ice and Snow World” by leveraging its abundant ice and snow resources；“让游客在欣赏冰雪之美的同时也能体验当地独特的民俗文化”是补充说明性内容，表示动作，且逻辑主语即整个句子的主语“哈尔滨”，故翻译为现在分词短语，充当伴随状语，即allowing visitors to appreciate the beauty of ice and snow while experiencing the region's unique folk culture，注意“在……的同时”强调“在……的过程中同时进行另一项活动”，需使用while连接；句首的“例如”翻译为For example或For instance。\n3. 第三句：主体句是“曾令人畏惧的冰天雪地正吸引着四面八方的游客”，其中“曾令人畏惧的冰天雪地”可翻译为The once-feared frozen wilderness、The formerly daunting ice-and-snow landscape或What was once an intimidating frozen landscape，“正吸引着四面八方的游客”翻译为is now attracting tourists from all directions；“成为深受欢迎的旅游胜地”表示补充说明，是伴随情况，翻译为现在分词短语becoming a highly popular tourist destination，“旅游胜地”还可翻译为tourist attraction。\n4. 第四句：“冰雪旅游业”翻译为The ice and snow tourism industry；谓语“正为当地的经济发展做出越来越大的贡献”翻译为is making an increasingly significant contribution to local economic development。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2025-06-3","source":"2025年06月 · 第3套","prompt":"近年来，中国越来越多的城市着力打造“15分钟便民生活圈(convenient living circles)”。社区居民步行15分钟就能享受到日常所需的公共服务。生活圈内建有便利店、公园、健身场地、图书馆、学校、社区食堂、诊所等。生活圈的建立能够为居民提供更加便利、舒适、友好、愉悦的生活环境，更好地满足城市居民多元化的日常生活服务需求，提升居民的生活品质和幸福感。","ref":"In recent years, an increasing number of cities in China have been focusing on building the “15-minute convenient living circles”. Local communities can access daily public services within a 15-minute walk. These living circles include facilities such as convenience stores, parks, fitness areas, libraries, schools, community canteens, and clinics. These living circles are built to provide residents with a more convenient, comfortable, friendly, and enjoyable living environment, better meeting the needs of diverse everyday services of urban dwellers while enhancing their quality of life and sense of happiness.","tips":"1. “近年来”翻译为In recent years；“越来越多的”可翻译为an increasing number of或more and more，前者是首选；翻译“着力打造‘15分钟便民生活圈’”时，应注意使用现在完成时或现在完成进行时，呼应句首的“近年来”这一完成时标志性的时间状语，故可译为have been focusing on building the “15-minute convenient living circles”或having focused on building the “15-minute convenient living circles”，现在完成进行时更强调过去到现在的持续进行的状态。\n2. 第二句：“步行15分钟”在此时为状语，可翻译为介词短语within a 15-minute walk；“享受到日常所需的公共服务”可翻译为can access daily public services，can have access to或can enjoy convenient access to everyday public services等。\n3. 第三句：“生活圈内”可以直接翻译为“内”，用“生活圈”，即These living circles作主语；当然，也可以不译，直接翻译为状语，即Within these circles。后一句中，后面的内容“建有便利店、公园、健身场地、图书馆、学校、社区食堂、诊所等”应使用there be句型来表达，即there are facilities such as convenience stores, parks, fitness areas, libraries, schools, community canteens, and clinics，或者添加主语“人们”，将其翻译为people build facilities such as…；不过综合来看，后一情况中的两种翻译方式都不如第一种省译情况更直接了，更符合英文表达习惯。\n4. 第四句：本句较长，可先分析句子逻辑关系，进行拆分后再逐一翻译。通过分析可知，“生活圈的建立能够为居民提供更加便利、舒适、友好、愉悦的生活环境”是主体，翻译为These living circles are built to provide residents with a more convenient, comfortable, friendly, and enjoyable living environment；“更好地满足城市居民多元化的日常生活服务需求”和“提升居民的生活品质和幸福感”是并列关系，表示同时存在的情况，可使用while连接，联系主体句的内容，后面的两个并列分句共同充当伴随状语，应使用现在分词短语来翻译，即better meeting the needs of diverse everyday services of urban dwellers while enhancing their quality of life and sense of happiness。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2025-12-1","source":"2025年12月 · 第1套","prompt":"近年来，中国政府高度重视民营经济(private economy)的发展，出台了一系列政策支持民营企业。截至2025年3月底，全国民营企业数量超过5700万家，占企业总量的92.3%。民营企业不仅数量稳步增长，质量和结构也在不断提升。民营企业的研发投入不断增加，在新一代信息技术、人工智能等领域发展迅速。民营企业核心竞争力的增强为中国经济的高质量发展提供了有力支撑。","ref":"In recent years, the Chinese government has attached great importance to the development of the private economy and introduced a series of policies to support private enterprises. As of the end of March 2025, the number of private enterprises nationwide has exceeded 57 million, accounting for 92.3% of the total number. Private enterprises have achieved not only steady growth in quantity but also continuous improvement in quality and structure. With increasing investment in research and development, private enterprises have expanded rapidly in fields such as new-generation information technology and artificial intelligence. The enhanced core competitiveness of private enterprises has provided strong support for China's high-quality economic development.","tips":"1. 第一句：“近年来”翻译为In recent years；“高度重视”和“出台”并列，翻译成并列谓语动词，即has attached great importance to and introduced。\n2. 第二句：“占企业总量的92.3%”表示伴随情况，翻译成现在分词短语，即accounting for 92.3% of the total number。\n3. 第三句：“不仅数量稳步增长，质量和结构也在不断提升”含有“不仅……而且……”的并列结构，翻译为have achieved not only steady growth in quantity but also continuous improvement in quality and structure。\n4. 第四句：“研发投入不断增加”是“在新一代信息技术、人工智能等领域发展迅速”的原因或背景信息，前者可翻译成with结构，即With increasing investment in research and development，后者翻译为private enterprises have expanded rapidly in fields such as new-generation information technology and artificial intelligence。\n5. 第五句：句子主语是“民营企业核心竞争力的增强”，翻译为The enhanced core competitiveness of private enterprises；“为中国经济的高质量发展提供了有力支撑”为谓语和宾语部分，翻译为has provided strong support for China's high-quality economic development。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2025-12-2","source":"2025年12月 · 第2套","prompt":"近年来，“城市漫步(city walk)”在中国的年轻人中悄然兴起，已成为一种旅游新潮流。与传统旅游不同，城市漫步不追求在短时间内游览尽可能多的景点，而是随意行走或按照主题路线漫步在城市的大街小巷。漫步者品尝地道小吃，欣赏特色建筑，了解当地生活方式。他们还用相机或手机记录城市的风景和人物。这种旅游方式能让城市漫步者更深入了解城市的历史与文化。","ref":"In recent years, “city walk” has quietly emerged among young people in China, becoming a new travel trend. Unlike traditional tourism, city walk does not aim to visit as many attractions as possible in a short period. Instead, it involves strolling casually or following themed routes through the streets and alleys of a city. Walkers sample local snacks, admire distinctive architecture, and learn about the local way of life. They also capture the city's scenery and people with cameras or smartphones. This form of travel allows city walkers to gain a deeper understanding of the city's history and culture.","tips":"1. 第一句：句子的谓语“在中国的年轻人中悄然兴起”翻译为has quietly emerged among young people in China；“已成为一种旅游新潮流”表示伴随情况或结果，翻译成现在分词短语，即becoming a new travel trend。\n2. 第二句：“不追求在短时间内游览尽可能多的景点”是句子的谓语和宾语部分，翻译为does not aim to visit as many attractions as possible in a short period；“而是随意行走或按照主题路线漫步在城市的大街小巷”翻译为单独的句子，即Instead, it involves strolling casually or following themed routes through the streets and alleys of a city。\n3. 第三句：句子的谓语和宾语部分由三个并列短语构成，即“品尝地道小吃”“欣赏特色建筑”和“了解当地生活方式”，翻译为sample local snacks, admire distinctive architecture, and learn about the local way of life。\n4. 第四句：“记录”翻译成capture（意为“拍摄；捕获”），比record更贴切，更生动，能体现“捕捉瞬间”的感觉。\n5. 第五句：“这种旅游方式”是句子主语，翻译为This form of travel；“能让城市漫步者更深入了解城市的历史与文化”是句子的谓语和宾语部分，翻译为allows city walkers to gain a deeper understanding of the city's history and culture，使用了allow sb. to do sth.（允许某人做某事）的结构。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2025-12-3","source":"2025年12月 · 第3套","prompt":"中国政府十分重视绿色经济的发展。通过加强森林资源保护、加大污染治理力度等一系列措施，许多地区的生态环境得到了显著改善。绿水青山(lucid waters and lush mountains)促进了当地的旅游、健康等产业的发展，创造了可观的经济效益。如今，生态环境与人类社会和谐共存的观念在中国已深入人心。绿色经济的推进不仅能为中国可持续发展做出贡献，也为全球环境保护提供了宝贵经验。","ref":"The Chinese government places great emphasis on the development of the green economy. Through a series of measures, such as strengthening the protection of forest resources and intensifying pollution control, the ecological environment in many regions has been significantly improved. Lucid waters and lush mountains have boosted the growth of local industries like tourism and healthcare, generating substantial economic benefits. Today, the concept of harmonious coexistence between the ecological environment and human society has taken deep root in China. The advancement of the green economy not only contributes to China's sustainable development but also provides valuable experience for global environmental protection.","tips":"1. 第一句：“十分重视”除了可翻译为places great emphasis on，还可翻译为attaches great importance to等。\n2. 第二句：“通过……一系列措施”翻译成介词短语，即Through a series of measures, such as strengthening the protection of forest resources and intensifying pollution control；“许多地区的生态环境得到了显著改善”是句子主干，翻译为the ecological environment in many regions has been significantly improved。\n3. 第三句：“绿水青山促进了……”为句子主干，翻译为Lucid waters and lush mountains have boosted the growth of local industries like tourism and healthcare；“创造了可观的经济效益”表示结果，可翻译成现在分词短语，即generating substantial economic benefits，作结果状语。\n4. 第四句：“生态环境与人类社会和谐共存的观念”是句子主语，翻译为the concept of harmonious coexistence between the ecological environment and human society；“在中国已深入人心”是谓语部分，翻译为has taken deep root in China。\n5. 第五句：“绿色经济的推进”是句子的主语，翻译为The advancement of the green economy；“不仅……也……”翻译为并列结构not only…but also…；“为中国可持续发展做出贡献”翻译为contributes to China's sustainable development；“为全球环境保护提供了宝贵经验”翻译为provides valuable experience for global environmental protection。","tipsLabel":"译点精析"},{"id":"2026-06-1","source":"2026年06月 · 第1套","prompt":"中国有句老话：“一日为师，终身为父”。在中国人的观念里，老师不仅传授知识，更教给学生做人的道理。在古代，学生初次见老师时要举行隆重的仪式，足见老师地位之高。为弘扬尊师的优良传统，中国从1985年开始将每年的9月10日定为教师节。在这一天，学生以各种方式表达对老师的敬意。尊师是中华民族的传统美德，在当今社会得到了发扬光大。","ref":"As an old Chinese saying goes, “A teacher for a day is a father for a lifetime.” In the mindset of Chinese people, a teacher not only imparts knowledge but also teaches students the principles of being a good person. In ancient times, students held a solemn ceremony when they first met their teachers, which fully shows the high status of teachers. Therefore, to promote the fine tradition of respecting teachers, China has designated September 10th as Teachers’ Day since 1985. On this day, students express their respect for their teachers in various ways. Respecting teachers is a traditional virtue of the Chinese nation, which has been carried forward and greatly enhanced in today’s society.","tips":"1. 中国有句老话：“一日为师，终身为父。”本句描述的是普遍认可的真理，在英语中，表达谚语、科学事实或普遍真理时，通常使用一般现在时；中文原句无被动含义，因此译文使用主动语态，句子结构较为简单，顺译即可。“中国有句老话”可译为As an old Chinese saying goes或There is an old saying in China；“一日为师，终身为父”可简译为A teacher for a day is a father for a lifetime，也可以遵照其含义，译为One who teaches you, even for a single day, deserves the lifelong respect you give your own father。\n2. 在中国人的观念里，老师不仅传授知识，更教给学生做人的道理。本句描述的是普遍观念，属于客观表达，因此译文使用一般现在时；主语是动作（传授、教给）的执行者，因此译文使用主动语态。“在中国人的观念里”处理为介词短语作状语，置于句首；“不仅……更……”使用not only…but also…结构，本句顺译即可。“在……的观念里”可译为in the mindset/eyes/conception/perception of…；“传授知识”可译为impart knowledge或pass on knowledge；“教给学生做人的道理”中的“做人”不可直接译为being a human，在该句语境中是指在社会、伦理、道德层面成为一个合格、得体、有修养的人，“道理”则指其中的准则、原则和智慧，因此可译为teaches students the principles of being a good person。\n3. 在古代，学生初次见老师时要举行隆重的仪式，足见老师地位之高。本句可拆分为两个逻辑层次：一是事实描述，即“在古代，学生初次见老师时要举行隆重的仪式”；二是结论评述，即“足见老师地位之高”。翻译时可将事实描述作为主句，结论评述处理成which引导的非限制性定语从句。由“在古代”“初次”可知，主句需使用一般过去时，且主语“学生”是动作的执行者，因此主句使用主动语态；“老师地位之高”是一种普遍的社会观念和认知，因此which引导的非限制性定语从句需使用一般现在时。“在古代”可译为In ancient times或In olden times；“举行”译为hold；“隆重的仪式”可译为a solemn/grand/formal ceremony；“足见”可以理解为“完全可以看出/足以说明”，译为fully show/reflect/indicate/demonstrate；“老师地位之高”可译为the high status of teachers，也可以翻译成含有感叹语气的表达，即how high teachers' status is。\n4. 为弘扬尊师的优良传统，中国从1985年开始将每年的9月10日定为教师节。由“从1985年开始”可知，动作从1985年开始，一直持续到现在，且可能继续下去，因此译文使用现在完成时更合适；如果用一般过去时，只表示“1985年那年定下了”，无法体现“一直延续到现在”的状态。主语“中国”是动作“定为”的执行者，因此译文使用主动语态；“为弘扬尊师的优良传统”是后续动作的目的，因此处理为不定式短语作目的状语，置于句首；“中国从……教师节”作为主句，“从1985年开始”为时间状语，置于句尾。在本句译文最开头可加表示因果关系的逻辑关系词Therefore，使本句与第3句衔接更加紧密。“为……”可译为To do…或In order to do…；“……的优良传统”可译为the fine tradition of…；“尊师”即“尊重老师”，译为respect teachers；“从……（时间）开始”译为since+时间点；“将……定为……”可译为designate…as…或establish…as…或set…as…；“教师节”有固定的英文表达，即Teachers' Day。\n5. 在这一天，学生以各种方式表达对老师的敬意。本句描述一个反复发生的规律性行为，即每年的教师节都是如此，因此译文使用一般现在时；主语“学生”是动作“表达”的执行者，因此译文使用主动语态即可。本句为简单句，译文可处理为“时间状语+主谓宾+方式状语”的结构。“在这一天”处理成介词短语作时间状语，置于句首；“学生”为主语；“表达”为谓语；“对老师的敬意”为宾语；“以各种方式”处理成介词短语作方式状语，置于句尾。“在这一天”译为On this day即可；“以各种方式”可译为in various/different ways或in a variety of ways；“表达对某人的敬意”可译为express/show respect for sb.。\n6. 尊师是中华民族的传统美德，在当今社会得到了发扬光大。本句可拆分为两个逻辑层次：一是信息陈述核心事实，即“尊师是中华民族的传统美德”；二是补充信息，进一步解释说明核心事实，即“在当今社会得到了发扬光大”。因此可将主信息作为主句，翻译成“主系表”结构；将补充信息处理成which引导的非限制性定语从句。主句描述的是普遍事实，因此译文使用一般现在时；which引导的非限制性定语从句强调从过去到现在这一美德得以延续和发展，且对当下有影响，因此该部分使用现在完成时更合适；“得到发扬光大”隐含“被（社会/人们）发扬光大”的含义，因此该部分需使用被动语态。“中华民族”译为the Chinese nation；“传统美德”可译为traditional virtue；“得到了发扬光大”应理解为“不仅保留下来了，而且做得更好、影响更大”，译为be carried forward and greatly enhanced。","tipsLabel":"翻译点拨"},{"id":"2026-06-2","source":"2026年06月 · 第2套","prompt":"餐桌礼仪（dining etiquette）是中华传统文化的重要组成部分，蕴含着热情有礼的待客之道。为了招待客人，主人会根据客人的口味和喜好准备丰富精致的菜肴。就餐座位的安排非常讲究，主人坐在正对大门的位置，在主人身边就座的是最重要的客人。进餐时，主人会不时地为客人添酒加菜。这种独特的餐桌礼仪已延续了数千年，对促进和谐的人际交往起到了重要作用。","ref":"Dining etiquette is an important part of traditional Chinese culture, embodying a warm and polite way of hospitality. To entertain guests, hosts prepare abundant and exquisite dishes based on the guests’ tastes and preferences. In addition, the seating arrangement at a meal is very particular: the host takes the seat directly facing the door, and the most important guests sit next to the host. During the meal, the host will refill the guests’ glasses and add food to their plates from time to time. This unique dining etiquette has lasted for thousands of years and has played a significant role in promoting harmonious interpersonal communication.","tips":"1. 餐桌礼仪（dining etiquette）是中华传统文化的重要组成部分，蕴含着热情有礼的待客之道。本句是对餐桌礼仪的客观描述，译文使用一般现在时即可，全句无被动含义，因此使用主动语态。分析句意可知，分句一“餐桌礼仪……部分”可作为主句，处理为“主系表”结构；分句二“蕴含着……之道”可处理为现在分词短语作伴随状语，对主句进行补充说明。“中华传统文化”可译为traditional Chinese culture；“……的重要组成部分”可译为an important part of…；“蕴含”可译为embody；“热情有礼的”可译为warm and polite；“待客之道”可译为way of hospitality，或者直接译为hospitality，这个词本身指的就是“待客的好意、行为、方式”。\n2. 为了招待客人，主人会根据客人的口味和喜好准备丰富精致的菜肴。本句陈述的是一般性的文化习俗，英文通常使用一般现在时；主语“主人”是动作“准备”的发出者，因此译文使用主动语态。本句结构清晰，“为了招待客人”表示目的，处理为不定式短语作目的状语；“主人”为主语；“准备”为谓语；“丰富精致的菜肴”为宾语；“根据客人的口味和喜好”可以处理为过去分词短语（based on…）作后置定语，解释说明菜肴是按照什么标准准备的，也可以处理为介词短语（according to…）作状语，置于句尾。“招待客人”可译为entertain/host/treat guests；“主人”译为host即可；“根据”可译为（be）based on…或according to…；“客人的口味和喜好”可译为the guests' tastes and preferences；“丰富精致的”可译为abundant and exquisite或rich and fine；“菜肴”可译为dishes。\n3. 就餐座位的安排非常讲究，主人坐在正对大门的位置，在主人身边就座的是最重要的客人。本句描述的是中国餐桌文化中普遍存在的礼仪规则，属于常态性的描述，因此译文使用一般现在时，全句无被动含义，因此使用主动语态。本句由三个分句组成，分句一总述就餐座位安排的特点，分句二和分句三具体说明座位是如何安排的，因此分句一后用冒号引出分句二和分句三的内容，分句二和分句三用并列连词and连接即可。此外，为了使句子间的衔接更加紧密，可以在本句开头添加表示递进关系的逻辑关系词In addition、Moreover或Furthermore等。“就餐座位”可译为seating arrangement at a meal或dining seating arrangement；“安排”译为arrangement即可；“讲究”可译为particular；“坐在正对大门的位置”可译为takes the seat directly facing the door或sits directly facing the door；“在主人身边就座的是最重要的客人”即“最重要的客人坐在主人旁边”，“在（某人）身边就座”可译为sit next to sb.或sit beside sb.。\n4. 进餐时，主人会不时地为客人添酒加菜。本句描述中国餐桌礼仪中的习惯性行为，翻译时可用一般现在时，也可用will表示习惯性的行为，体现“在这种场合下通常会这样做”的含义；主语“主人”是动作的发出者，因此译文使用主动语态。“进餐时”处理为介词短语作时间状语，置于句首；“主人”为主语；“不时地”作频率状语；“添”“加”为谓语；“酒”“菜”为宾语。“进餐时”可译为During the meal；“不时地”可译为from time to time或occasionally；“为客人添酒加菜”可理解为往客人杯中加酒使其由不满变为满、往客人盘中添加菜肴，因此可译为refill the guests' glasses and add food to their plates。\n5. 这种独特的餐桌礼仪已延续了数千年，对促进和谐的人际交往起到了重要作用。本句由两个分句组成，可处理为由and连接的并列句，共用同一个主语“这种独特的餐桌礼仪”。分句一中由“已”可知动作从过去开始持续到现在，且可能继续延续；分句二中“起到了重要作用”表示从过去到现在一直在起作用且对当下仍有意义，因此两个分句的译文均使用现在完成时；主语执行“延续”和“起作用”两个动作，均使用主动语态。“独特的”可译为unique或distinctive；“延续了数千年”可译为last for thousands of years；“对……起到了重要作用”可译为play a significant role in或play an important role in；“促进”可译为promote或foster；“和谐的”可译为harmonious；“人际交往”可译为interpersonal communication。","tipsLabel":"翻译点拨"},{"id":"2026-06-3","source":"2026年06月 · 第3套","prompt":"在中国传统文化中，亲朋好友之间互赠礼物是人际交往的一种重要礼节（etiquette）。赠送礼物不仅是物质的馈赠，更是情感的表达，是维系人际关系的重要纽带。一份精心挑选、符合接受者喜好的礼物，往往能加深彼此的感情。中国人遵循“礼尚往来”（mutually exchanging courtesies）的传统，接受礼物时会表达谢意，并适时回赠礼物，以增进彼此的融洽关系。","ref":"In traditional Chinese culture, exchanging gifts among friends and relatives is an important etiquette in interpersonal communication. Giving gifts is not merely a material offering but also an expression of emotion, serving as an important bond that maintains interpersonal relationships. Therefore, a carefully selected gift that caters to the recipient’s preferences can often deepen mutual affection. The Chinese follow the tradition of “mutually exchanging courtesies”: when receiving a gift, they express gratitude and return a gift at an appropriate time, so as to enhance the harmonious relationship with one another.","tips":"1. 在中国传统文化中，亲朋好友之间互赠礼物是人际交往的一种重要礼节（etiquette）。本句描述的是客观事实，不是过去、现在或未来的具体事件，因此译文使用一般现在时；“是”表明该句使用系表结构，为主动语态。本句为“地点状语+主系表”结构：“在中国传统文化中”处理为介词短语作地点状语，限定互赠礼物的文化背景；“亲朋好友之间互赠礼物”为主语，其中核心表达为“互赠礼物”，处理为动名词，“亲朋好友之间”处理为介词短语作后置定语；“是”为系动词；“人际交往的一种重要礼节”为表语，其中“一种重要礼节”为核心表达，“人际交往的”可以理解为“在人际交往方面”，处理为介词短语作后置定语。“中国传统文化”译为traditional Chinese culture；“亲朋好友”即“朋友和亲戚”，可译为friends and relatives；“互赠礼物”可译为exchange gifts或give gifts to each other；“人际交往”可译为interpersonal communication。\n2. 赠送礼物不仅是物质的馈赠，更是情感的表达，是维系人际关系的重要纽带。本句描述的是“赠送礼物”这一行为的本质属性和社会功能，因此译文使用一般现在时；三个“是”表明该句使用系表结构，为主动语态。本句由三个分句组成，分句一和分句二描述赠送礼物的本质属性，属于一个意群，分句三是对其社会功能的描述，属于一个独立的意群。因此可以将分句一、二分作为主句，其中“不仅……，更……”用not only…but also…结构；分句三处理成现在分词短语作伴随状语，其主干为“是重要纽带”，“维系人际关系”可处理为定语从句，修饰“纽带”。“赠送礼物”可译为giving gifts；“物质的馈赠”可译为a material offering；“情感的表达”可译为an expression of emotion；“维系人际关系”可译为maintain/sustain interpersonal relationships；“纽带”可译为bond。\n3. 一份精心挑选、符合接受者喜好的礼物，往往能加深彼此的感情。本句描述的是礼物对人的情感产生的普遍作用，属于客观事实，因此译文使用一般现在时；主语“礼物”发出“加深”这个动作，因此译文使用主动语态。本句为“主谓宾”结构，主语较长，可以将“一份精心挑选的礼物”作为主语核心词，将“符合接受者喜好”处理为定语从句；“能加深”为谓语；“彼此的感情”为宾语。本句与第2句暗含因果关系，第2句为“因”，本句为“果”，因此可以在本句译文的句首添加表示因果关系的逻辑关系词，如Therefore、Thus或As a result。“精心挑选”可译为carefully selected/chosen；“符合……喜好”可译为cater to someone's preferences或suit someone's preferences；“接受者”可译为recipient或receiver；“加深彼此的感情”可译为deepen mutual affection。\n4. 中国人遵循“礼尚往来”（mutually exchanging courtesies）的传统，接受礼物时会表达谢意，并适时回赠礼物，以增进彼此的融洽关系。本句描述的是中国人的常规文化习惯和普遍行为模式，译文使用一般现在时即可；主语“中国人”是动作的执行者，因此使用主动语态。本句为复合句，句子主干为“中国人遵循‘礼尚往来’的传统”，可处理为“主谓宾”结构；“接受……并适时……”是对“礼尚往来”这一行为的具体解释，可用冒号引出，该部分无主语，翻译时需要添加主语，由前面的“中国人”可知主语也是“中国人”，为避免重复可以使用人称代词they；“以增进彼此的融洽关系”是这一行为的目的，处理为目的状语。“中国人”可译为The Chinese，作整体概念；“遵循……的传统”可译为follow the tradition of…；“接受礼物”可译为receive a gift；“表达谢意”可译为express/show gratitude；“适时”即可译为at an appropriate time或at a proper time；“回赠礼物”可译为return a gift或give a gift in return；“增进彼此的融洽关系”可译为enhance/strengthen the harmonious relationship with one another。","tipsLabel":"翻译点拨"}]
